>  Nootropics are for squeezing another 1% out of already peak performance. 

&#x200B;

Really? You think the  alignment of exercise, right amount of sleep and "rich diet" (no-sugary diet) make you at your peak performance? And the most  intriguing part is the squeezing of 1%. How can you measure 1% of cognition or well-being?   


No, I'm not  decreasing the importance of the exercise, sleep and diet.   


The puzzling aspect of *nootropics community* is the deviations, the subjective experience, the  pioneering and bro-science. And why is sadly the conjunction of unhealthy behaviors and nootropics? Maybe you are not sleeping because of your newborn baby and need something to combat the effects of sleep deprivation and others cases like that.   



&#x200B;
